<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  MFC PlotJuggler layout. Curves are keyed against the mirrored message schema,
  so the same template lines up leaf-for-leaf across the two feeds:

    ivy server  (sw/ground_segment/tmtc/server.ml)  UDP/JSON port 9870
                root = "Hoops_111_MFC (111)" / <MSG> / <field>
    nps_scope   (sw/simulator/nps/nps_scope.c)       UDP/JSON, scope_port flag (default 9871)
                root = "Hoops_111_MFC (sim)" / [MSG|TRUTH|EST|SENSORS|SP|MODE] / field

  Shared controller branches (STAB_MFC, GUIDANCE_MFC, WLS_V/U, and the
  GUIDANCE_MFC_ACC2ATT debug message — sim branch "ACC2ATT") carry BOTH roots'
  paths so the layout works for either or both feeds; absent series just don't
  draw. Sim-only branches (TRUTH, EST, SENSORS, SP, MODE) use the (sim) root.

  To stream both feeds at once, add two UDP-Server instances under the UDP Server
  plugin: one on 9870 (ivy) and one on the sim scope_port. NOTE: sim timestamp
  is sim time (fdm.time); ivy timestamp is wall-clock — the two roots will not
  share an absolute x-axis when shown together.
-->
